-- Based on SPE1CASE2, modified to have a gas cap of undersaturated wet gas
-- (VAPOIL) in the top layer above undersaturated oil.  The producer is
-- controlled by observed (history) surface rates converted to reservoir
-- voidage rate (WCONHIST RESV), with an observed GOR exceeding the average
-- dissolved GOR of the oil, and an observed OGR exceeding the average
-- vaporised OGR of the gas.  The conversion of the surface rates to
-- reservoir voidage therefore depends on the average dissolved GOR and
-- vaporised OGR used, and whether cells without oil (gas) contribute to
-- the average dissolved GOR (vaporised OGR).  The observed rates are
-- monthly averages from a run of the same model with the producer on oil
-- rate control.

RUNSPEC

TITLE
   SPE1 - CASE 2 - WET GAS CAP, WCONHIST RESV

DIMENS
   10 10 3 /

EQLDIMS
/

TABDIMS
/

OIL
GAS
WATER
DISGAS
VAPOIL

FIELD

START
   1 'JAN' 2015 /

WELLDIMS
   1 1 1 1 /

UNIFIN
UNIFOUT

GRID

INIT

DX
   300*1000 /
DY
   300*1000 /
DZ
   100*20 100*30 100*50 /

BOX
   1 10 1 10 1 1 /
TOPS
   100*8325 /
ENDBOX

PORO
   300*0.3 /

PERMX
   100*500 100*50 100*200 /
PERMY
   100*500 100*50 100*200 /
-- Low vertical permeability in the middle layer limits gas coning
-- from the gas cap into the producer.
PERMZ
   100*500 100*0.1 100*200 /

